   "etymology": "From a phonetic collapse of two Proto-Albanian terms, *per(i) and *pra, the former from Proto-Indo-European *péri (“leading (out) across or around”) and *pér (“through”) (compare Sanskrit परि (parí, “(a)round”)), the latter from Proto-Indo-European *pró (“towards, before”) (compare Ancient Greek πρό (pró, “before, forwards”). Possibly reinforced by Latin per (“through, over”).",
